    "goal": "Report the binary .bed size and per-chromosome .bed size for a GWAS genotype dataset of 5482 samples and 9523103 variants (1227924 on the largest chromosome).",
    "rationale": "Pure sizing calculation for a PLINK binary genotype dataset. The .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant, so total size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB, and per-chromosome size uses the same rule applied to the largest chromosome's variant count. No experimental design is involved; this is a disk/time budget estimate for downstream GWAS analysis.",
